WEBVTT

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:47.550
Fascinatingly, I do believe the Japanese people have an eye for ascertaining beauty and charm,

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:52.290
as well as holding such things dear to their hearts.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:55.630
Isabella L. Bird
( 1831-1904 )

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:21.790
"When a man Loves a woman."

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.670
And also the reverse.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.130
It's no different for those of the same sex.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:45.140
The desire to always be with the one you love is nature's law.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.980
It's instinct.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.820
So, Yanagi, what exactly are these?

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.610
Isn't it obvious?

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.950
They're for sale.  For S.A.L.E.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.070
You going to sell these things again this year?

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.840
Didn't you do the same thing last year?

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.910
There's demand, you see.  Demand.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.460
The wish to always be able to gaze at the one you love...

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:28.240
In this brutal world, it's thriving on that warmth that keeps people fighting on each and every day.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.490
Dreaming of their yet-unfulfilled future, imagining their yet unseen progeny...

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:35.020
The possibility of genes leading to such beauty etching into their hearts...

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.060
This sublime calling only allowed to us youth!

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.450
I cannot disavow such demand!

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.290
Indeed, I believe it is something that needs encouraging!

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.530
Demand, huh?

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.490
Well, I guess it's not like I can't see how that works.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.070
Someone wants a certain someone's picture.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.450
Someone else wants another certain someone's picture, etc.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:59.810
As youth goes, so goes my proceeds!

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.590
The numbers are like jewels!

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.550
You really like money, don't you, Yanagi?

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.180
Honestly, yes, I like money.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.020
However, is that really so evil?

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:19.210
It is possible there are those that whisper of me taking advantage of people's true desires to provide for myself.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.940
Just let them talk.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:27.910
For it is exactly that motivation born from libido that grew the cultural and history of humanity!

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:32.940
And modern society still requires such incentive, such impetus!

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.460
I-I get it already...

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.680
But are you sure this is okay?

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.210
What about getting consent to be photographed?

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.270
That's kind of a delicate issue so I'm not gonna get into it.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.330
Hey now...

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.210
Oh, there's a lot of new faces here.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:49.430
Well, of course.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.710
Most of them are new students.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:52.720
Saywha?!

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.060
In other words, they're new merchandise.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.890
The marketplace constantly demands new merchandise!

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:03.550
That's just the fundamentals of good business practice!

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.150
So it's all beginning again, huh?

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:09.740
But be that as it may, you work really damn fast.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.780
Oh, I've got those bases covered.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.410
I've got me a cute little first year to gather info for me.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.890
That's one bad example you set.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.090
Birds of a feather?

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:24.130
I collect types like myself who share my goals as my comrades.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:27.810
Don't you think "Photo Shop Yanagi" has a nice ring to it?

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.820
That's totally lame sounding.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.130
Y-Yanagi...

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:37.730
Who is this?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:38.730
Who is this girl?

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.040
Which one?

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.280
Oh, her.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.990
Um, just a second here...

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:55.160
That's first year, class 6, Nonomura Ayumi-chan.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.750
Hey, please don't take my picture without asking!

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.710
Take her picture, take her picture!

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.380
Take my picture too!

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.920
Stop being so shy.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.890
Me too!  Me too!

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:09.440
Hey, stop messin' up the shot, you're annoying!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.640
Okay, Yumippe.  Smile!

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:12.990
Sheesh...

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:16.090
Nonomura Ayumi-chan, huh?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.970
Yes.  She is quite popular among the first years.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.900
She is quite the cutey, I believe.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.740
Speaking of which, the level is quite high for this year's...

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.240
Don't you like this Iizuka girl?

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.870
Hey, are you listening?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.910
Indeed, she...

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.580
Yes...

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.860
Indeed she is truly...

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.190
...a blessing sent from heaven.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.570
My angel...

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.020
Angel

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.020
Fool

00:06:57.130 --> 00:07:00.730
I realized this back when we were first years, but you're an idiot, aren't you?

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.870
Yes, I am an idiot.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:12.530
My heart was overtaken by an angel, and I forgot my own mission.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:17.590
What foolishness... This grand idiot can only but laugh...

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:22.450
No, that's <i>not</i> what I meant!

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:25.580
Yeah, he's kind of a moron like that.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:30.340
Well, to me he's...

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.680
Um, I know it's funny, but listen.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:40.180
Ah, but I know he's a decent guy, so if you could help me out...

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:44.540
Well, like sure, I'm okay with that.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.150
But I wonder what she'd say if you told her that.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.880
Yeah...

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:54.750
Yumippe is kind of a late-bloomer when it comes to these things, so she'd never know unless you told her.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.340
Is the photography club room over this way?

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:19.410
500 yen.  Was that expensive?

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.930
Was it cheap?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:37.100
No, it was cheap.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:40.490
For her sake, such an expense is nothing!

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:46.460
Wai-!

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:53.720
D-Don't!

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:19.490
I'm sorry!  I'm sorry!  I'm sorry!  I'm sorry!  I'm sorry!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.080
It's okay, I'm fine.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.870
I'm just glad I fell from the second floor.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.790
And that there was brush to land on below.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.370
I'm sorry!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:29.070
Wait a second...

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:30.470
It's y-y-you!

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:46.560
U-Um, where might you have gotten this...

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.610
N-No, that's not it!  This isn't anything like...

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.350
I don't feel guilty or anything about having it!

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:59.330
Well, kinda.... No, but these are my real, true feelings!

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.870
I, Sengoku Shishimaru...

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:08.160
Am truly in love!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:15.420
And so I was confessed to just like that.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.570
Me, instead of you, Torako-san.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.550
What should you say back to him?

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:26.080
Hell if I know!  Never heard of him!

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.740
Way to go, Torako!

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:28.920
Go where?

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.100
Why did he confess to you anyway, Ayu?

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:35.110
That's what <i>I</i> want to know!

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.260
Well, whoever he is, he has poor taste.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.830
This girl.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:43.370
<i>That</i> one?!

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:45.950
Didn't I point to her in the first place?

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.260
It seems like she's actually called Torako-chan.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.060
Torako...

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.820
The name really suits her...

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.790
Oh, my angel!

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:26.030
This guy's a numskull.

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:29.660
Um, then I'll give you this picture.

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:31.960
Not for Sale

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:34.440
Hey!

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:36.530
Dude, are you still in middle school?

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.840
Some Days Later

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.840
Is it okay not to reply?

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.970
Let's go to karaoke on our way home today!

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:55.940
Takasaki

00:11:56.810 --> 00:12:00.440
Man, first period's already starting.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:03.570
I'm tired.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.480
And the bus ain't comin'.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.200
Might as well get somethin' to eat.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.580
Welcome!

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:58.940
The punk.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:17.940
She sure is late.  I wonder if Torako-san is coming to school today.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:21.040
It will be nice and quiet for a change.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.850
And Suzume-san, said...

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:24.740
Not a clue.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.600
...when I asked her.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:28.640
I wonder what she's doing?

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:56.730
Hey, where're ya goin'?

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.490
Uh, the bus stop is the other direction!

00:13:58.490 --> 00:13:59.560
Huh?

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.820
I said the bus stop is the other way!

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.820
Whatever, I ain't goin' to school today.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.270
It's lame.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.620
A true yankee (delinquent)!

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.000
Guess slackin' off is like the basics, yeah.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:10.740
Huh?

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.420
Well, punks gotta be punks.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:15.590
What's with you?

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:18.330
I ain't a yankee and I ain't no punk!

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:20.830
And why the hell are you followin' me?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.430
It's 'cause your parents are having a fight, right?

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:24.500
Like hell they are!

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:25.870
How prejudiced can you get?

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.250
And you have an upperclassman that runs a snack business.

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.090
There ain't no one like that!

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.720
You have a rally once a week!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.580
Doesn't happen!

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.670
A lone wolf?

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:37.140
You'd rather die than hang out with other people?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:40.220
The only person I don't wanna hang out with right now is <i>you</i>!

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:45.000
Boss, where's ya goin'?  Boss!

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.070
Why are you following me?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.820
I mean, stop following me!

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:51.770
Anyway, where should we go?  Karaoke sound good?

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.780
Are you just IGNORING me?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.290
Test, test!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.840
You're still here!

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.540
Huh, you say something?

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:03.750
You can sing first if you'd like.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:11.700
What number?

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.720
Fine, whatever.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:26.060
Note: Lengthy set of puns regarding the Chinese zodiac

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.640
Man, you really suck.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.310
Who gives a crap if I suck?

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.360
What matters is singing itself, man!

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:03.020
You'd better be some hot stuff if you can say that about other people!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.580
Hey now, hey now!

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.770
I'll make you regret sayin' that!

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.830
Call of you!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.620
<i>The tip of my toes miss a step</i>

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.250
<i>Twisting my ankle</i>

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:30.460
<i>My shoulder and the earth kiss violently.</i>

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.260
<i>I want to yell out, but "no cry"</i>

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:41.680
<i>I can't let people know the depth of the pain or my injury.</i>

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:44.310
<i>It's turning red, Ho ho!</i>

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.900
You suck just as bad as me!

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.860
I can't stand listening to it!

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:50.820
What'd you say, hothead?

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:54.900
Who you're callin' a hothead, with your tacky hairdo!

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:58.320
I called you a hothead 'cause you're a hothead!  Your voice could shatter glass!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.570
You're the one with the shrill voice!

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.610
You can't sing heavy metal with a voice like that!

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:04.190
I can't stand to listen to it!

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.500
It ain't like I was singing for you anyway!

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.000
Karaoke's about singin' your favorite songs!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:08.880
Are you dense?

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.360
It's lunchtime already.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:39.620
She obviously is not coming today.

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:56.240
I'm starving.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.650
What time is it?

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:00.180
Hell if I know.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:02.160
Wanna hit up a family restaurant?

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:03.690
Huh?

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.680
I ain't got that kind of money on me.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.940
Just pickin' somethin' up at a convenience store is fine.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:15.640
Welcome.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:20.840
Thank you, come again.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:42.760
Huh?  You're gonna eat <i>pudding</i>?

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.210
Got a problem with that?

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.020
I like sweet stuff.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.050
Some yankee you are.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.690
So yankees can't eat pudding?

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.880
Not like I really care.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:59.670
What's a yankee to you exactly anyway?

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:01.750
And I ain't a yankee anyway.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:03.170
Fine, whatever.

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:06.570
I'm a yankee, a real yankee.

00:19:12.990 --> 00:19:14.500
Ooh, it's a cat!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.710
And it's a tabby, too!

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:18.320
Aren't you the cute one?

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:25.150
You're really people friendly.

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:27.980
I know, I'll give you some of my salmon...

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:29.810
My salmon onigiri...

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:38.440
What?!

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.770
I like cats, okay!

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:43.630
You think it's weird for a yankee to like cats, huh?

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.640
It's fine!

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:49.700
Yankees always have a soft spot for animals after all, right?

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.680
Go ahead and hold him!

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:02.190
So cute!

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.940
What's your name anyway?

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:08.470
What's with that all of a sudden?

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:13.960
Makunouchi Ushio...

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:18.110
Ushio, you're so moe!

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:37.350
Okay, let's go to school!

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.960
Huh?  <i>Now</i>?

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.210
Why?

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:43.840
Well, I'm no yankee.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:46.760
And I like school.

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:50.560
I see.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:54.360
Then maybe I should go, too.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:55.780
I ain't a yankee either.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:57.370
Tell me your name, too.

00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:58.340
Nagatobimaru.

00:20:57.370 --> 00:21:02.400
Note:  Continuing references to "Ushio and Tora."

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.930
Huh?  Is that your family name?

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:02.390
Damn you, Hakumen no Mono!

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:04.300
What the hell are you talking about?

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.740
Where's your spear?  Your beast spear?

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:09.190
Spear?  What spear?

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:13.950
What were you two thinking?

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:16.160
Think you can just skip school?

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:19.130
And classes are already over for the day, idiots!

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.460
I've never met a bigger idiot than you in all my years as a teacher!

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.090
Torako-san...

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.560
And we were in the same class?

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:28.450
Are you listening?

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.550
She didn't notice...

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:42.210
My right hand has become flower vase!

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:45.930
Hey, I'm beggin' ya here, would you clean a little?

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:48.240
Is this the work of some youkai?!

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:22.210
Next time on Hyakko:

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:24.030
"Tigers on Three Sides."

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:25.840
Isn't that expression supposed to be "Neighbors on Three Sides?"

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:27.500
Let's pay a visit to Iizuka-senpai's house!

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:29.170
Tatsuki-oneechan's house!

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:29.930
And...

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:31.630
Look forward to next time!

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:32.410
What?  What?

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:33.430
What's going to happen?
